{
"dur": 51.865,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 13.08,
"text": "Now look at his 2026. In April came The Drama, an A24 film with Zendaya. It opened on Easter weekend against Mario, and still crossed a hundred million dollars worldwide in nineteen days.",
"end": 13.355
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 13.355,
"vo_start": 13.63,
"vo_end": 21.579,
"text": "A24 said more than eighty per cent of the audience came because of the two stars on the poster. That is the number that makes studio bosses pick up the phone.",
"end": 21.854
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 21.854,
"vo_start": 22.129,
"vo_end": 33.569,
"text": "Then in July, Christopher Nolan's The Odyssey. Pattinson played Antinous, the arrogant suitor trying to take Odysseus's house. It became Universal's biggest film of all time, passing Jurassic World.",
"end": 33.844
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 33.844,
"vo_start": 34.119,
"vo_end": 42.848,
"text": "In September he played the TV host Chris Hansen in Primetime. Critics loved it. The real Chris Hansen gave his performance a D on his own podcast.",
"end": 43.123
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 43.123,
"vo_start": 43.398,
"vo_end": 50.915,
"text": "And on the eighteenth of December, he's a shape-shifting villain in Dune: Part Three, for director Denis Villeneuve. Keep that name in mind too.",
"end": 51.865
}
],
